## Novopay Platform — Architect Standards (Java/XML)

**Domain:** Fintech lending (MFI). Money, compliance, audit. Low latency APIs; high throughput batches. No N+1. Traceable financial flows; fail-fast; idempotent writes.

**Modules:** accounting-v2, mfi-los, actor, payments, task, approval, authorization, audit, batch, dms, masterdata, notifications, api-gateway, reporting. Infra in `trustt-platform-lib/`. Orchestration XML owns transaction boundaries. Multi-tenant via `PlatformTenant` / `ThreadLocalContext`.

**Versions:** Spring Boot 3.5.6 (services) / 3.2.11 (infra); Java 17; Spring Cloud 2023.0.1; YugabyteDB; Gradle. Read `build.gradle` before implementing.

**Code style:** Records/DTOs; `var`; Optional; constructor injection; `@Slf4j`; Processors extend `AbstractProcessor`. ExecutionContext: `get*Value`, validate, `put` vs `putLocal`, no accidental overwrites. Errors: `NovopayFatalException` / `NovopayNonFatalException`; constants for codes; no silent swallow. DB: `nativeQuery=true`; soft-delete `is_deleted=false`; audit columns; orchestration-owned txns (rare `@Transactional`). Kafka: idempotency + Redis locks; tenant before process. Bank: JTF templates + WebClient decorator.

**API/contract:** Additive-only; grep all callers; uncertainty = breaking until reviewed.

**Git (multi-repo):** run git in service dir; commit often; no force-push shared; push origin only (DarpanSolanki), never upstream/trusttai.

**Implementation:** Minimal surface; backward compatible; error-proof; fast; idempotent. Tiered L0–L3 (see `architect-thinking.mdc` / skill). Docs: do not create unless asked; exception agent KB under `.cursor/`.

**Proactive flags (P1–P5):** platform-lib blast → warn; accounting schema → warn; bug fix → check gaps-digest; new event → event-registry hygiene; high-risk paths (DisbursementSyncService, LmsMessageBrokerConsumer, DisburseLoanAPIUtil, RedisCacheClient, InterestAccrualBookingBatchService, ProactiveExcessAmountRefundItemWriter) → state HIGH RISK ZONE + runbook.

**Auto-log DoD:** update accounting-flows / platform-lib / event-registry / gaps SoT / redis-key-registry / scheduler-registry / orchestration-map / knowledge-graph / changelog when touched. Output `Knowledge updated: […]`.
